# Skills Router & Manifest (`l1dder/skills.json`)

Before starting work, check the tables below and read the relevant `SKILL.md` files using the `Read` tool.
All project skills are managed declaratively via **`l1dder/skills.json`** (like `package.json` for AI Agent Skills).

## How to use

1. For workflow control (onboarding, ideas, features, roadmap planning, task execution, hotfixes), use the `L1DDER` control skills (`/l1-*` — Section 0).
2. For brainstorming, architecture design, TDD, bug diagnosis, and sprint reviews, read the engineering skills from Section 1 (`ponytail` + `mattpocock/skills` — **all bundled in `l1dder/skills/`!**).
3. Before writing code in `/l1-task`, `/l1-fast`, `/l1-hotfix` or `/l1-chore`, read the project stack skills from Section 2 (managed via the `"stack"` section in `l1dder/skills.json` and `npx l1dder skills install`).

**Important:** when a skill applies, read its `SKILL.md` via `Read` and follow it — do not just mention its name in `plan.md`.

